Based on my analysis:

```json
{
  "summary": "Added agentId to HTTP session titles, changing from hardcoded 'nezha-agent-session' to dynamic 'nezha-{agentId}'. This improves session traceability but lacks test coverage for the new behavior.",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "Testing singleton dependencies",
      "reminder": "When adding Config.getInstance() calls, always mock Config.getInstance() in tests to avoid external file dependencies (.nezha/agent-id.json)"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Request body verification",
      "reminder": "After modifying request payloads (like session title), add a test that verifies mockFetch was called with correct body structure"
    },
    {
      "topic": "Transport layer coupling",
      "reminder": "Avoid importing Config singleton in transport classes - prefer dependency injection for better testability"
    },
    {
      "topic": "vitest mock ordering",
      "reminder": "Use vi.mock() at module level or vi.mock('path') before test runs when mocking imports - vi.stubGlobal only works for globals like fetch"
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "location": "src/tests/UnifiedAgent.test.ts:54-65",
      "description": "Test 'should create session and return ID' doesn't verify the request body contains the agentId. After this change, the test is incomplete.",
      "fix": "Add assertion: expect(mockFetch).toHaveBeenCalledWith(expect.any(String), expect.objectContaining({ body: expect.stringContaining('nezha-') }))"
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "location": "src/core/transports/index.ts:141-146",
      "description": "No Config mock in test file. The existing tests will call Config.getInstance().getAgentId() which depends on .nezha/agent-id.json file existing.",
      "fix": "Add vi.mock('../../config/Config.js') and mock getAgentId() to return a predictable value"
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Consider injecting Config as a constructor parameter (optional) for HttpTransport to enable easier testing without mocking",
    "Add explicit test for concurrent session creation verifying unique agentId in each request",
    "Add test case for session creation with long agentId to verify no truncation issues"
  ],
  "praise": [
    "Good naming convention: 'nezha-{agentId}' is clear and consistent",
    "Dynamic session titles improve debugging and session identification",
    "Code follows existing patterns in the codebase"
  ],
  "overallScore": 72,
  "codeQualityScore": 85,
  "testCoverageScore": 45,
  "documentationScore": 80
}
```

**Key Takeaway**: The change itself is reasonable, but adding a singleton dependency (`Config.getInstance()`) without proper test mocking is a common pitfall. The existing tests likely still pass by accident (if `.nezha/agent-id.json` exists) but are now fragile.

